{"id":"claim:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--yar-valency-retaining-unexpressed-causee","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topics":["topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--causee"],"statement":{"en":"The indefinite causative suffix -yar/-ar retains the valency of the base verb because the causee cannot be overtly expressed as an NP or indexed on the verb.","ja":"不特定使役接尾辞-yar/-arは、被使役者を名詞句や人称標識として明示できないため、基底動詞の結合価を変化させない。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["-yar","-ar"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaevakobayashi2022@handbook-epub/l0100-30","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:bugaevakobayashi2022@handbook-epub/l0102-15","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--yar-avoids-specific-agent-mention","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topics":["topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--semantics"],"statement":{"en":"The causative suffix -yar is used to avoid specific mention of the agent.","ja":"使役接尾辞-yarは、動作主の明示的な言及を避けたい場合に用いられる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest/shizunai"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"assertive","conditions":[]},"forms":["-yar"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0180-09","stance":"asserts"},{"id":"stmt:refsing1986@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0181-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--the-sociative-prefixes-uko-and-uwe-originate-from","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topics":["topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar"],"statement":{"en":"The sociative prefixes uko- and uwe- originate from combinations of the reciprocal prefix u- with applicatives ko- and e-, and synchronically function as single valency-retaining markers meaning 'together'.","ja":"協調接頭辞uko-およびuwe-は、相互接頭辞u-と適用接頭辞ko-およびe-の結合に由来し、共時的には結合価を変化させずに「一緒に」という意味を付加する単一の標識として機能する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["uko-","uwe-"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaevakobayashi2022@handbook-epub/l0100-32","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--sociative-derivations-with-uko-are-much-more-frequent","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topics":["topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar"],"statement":{"en":"Sociative derivations with uko- are much more frequent than those with uwe-.","ja":"uko-による協調接頭辞派生は、uwe-による派生よりもはるかに頻度が高い。"},"type":"frequency","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["uko-","uwe-"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaevakobayashi2022@handbook-epub/l0100-33","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--sociative-derivations-from-1-argument-verbs-are-exclusively","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topics":["topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar"],"statement":{"en":"Sociative derivations from 1-argument verbs are exclusively subject-oriented, whereas those from 2-argument verbs can be either subject- or object-oriented depending on context.","ja":"1項動詞からの協調接頭辞派生は専ら主語指向であるのに対し、2項動詞からの派生は文脈に応じて主語指向にも目的語指向にもなりうる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["uko-","uwe-"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaevakobayashi2022@handbook-epub/l0100-34","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--the-sociative-meaning-together-can-also-be-expressed","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topics":["topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar"],"statement":{"en":"The sociative meaning 'together' can also be expressed by combining the reciprocal prefix u- with causative suffixes -re/-e/-te or -ka, mostly on intransitive bases.","ja":"「一緒に」という協調の意味は、相互接頭辞u-と使役接尾辞-re/-e/-teまたは-kaの結合によっても表され、その大部分は自動詞語幹から派生する。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":["mostly on intransitive bases"]},"forms":["u-","-re","-e","-te","-ka"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaevakobayashi2022@handbook-epub/l0100-35","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--the-indefinite-causative-suffix-yar-ar-does-not","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topics":["topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--causee"],"statement":{"en":"The indefinite causative suffix -yar/-ar does not change verbal valency.","ja":"不定使役接尾辞 -yar/-ar は動詞の価数を変化させない。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-yar","-ar"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2012@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0014-06","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--the-indefinite-causative-suffix-yar-ar-does-not-2","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topics":["topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--causee"],"statement":{"en":"The indefinite causative suffix -yar/-ar does not affect valency because the causee is indefinite and cannot be introduced as an argument.","ja":"不定人称使役接尾辞 -yar/-ar は、被使役者が不定であり項として導入され得ないため、結合価を変化させない。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/southwest"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-yar","-ar"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2012@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0022-07","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--the-indefinite-causative-in-yar-ar-is-often","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topics":["topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--causee"],"statement":{"en":"The indefinite causative in -yar/-ar is often used for politeness reasons to avoid mentioning the causee directly.","ja":"-yar/-arによる不特定使役は、被使役者を直接言及しないことが好ましい場合に待遇上の理由からしばしば用いられる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"usually","modality":"actual","conditions":["for politeness reasons"]},"forms":["-yar","-ar"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaevakobayashi2022@handbook-epub/l0102-16","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--the-causative-suffix-yar-expresses-plurality-of-the","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topics":["topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--causee"],"statement":{"en":"The causative suffix -yar expresses plurality of the causee, and after stems ending in r, it drops y to become -ar.","ja":"使役される者の複数を表す形式に -yar があり、この -yar は r で終わる語幹の後では y を脱落させて -ar となる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-yar","-ar"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:kindaichi1936@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0136-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--affixes-that-do-not-change-arity-include-affiliative","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topics":["topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--causee"],"statement":{"en":"Affixes that do not change arity include affiliative-equivalent nominal prefixes, adverbial prefixes, the causative suffix -yar, and the plural suffix -pa.","ja":"アリティを増減させない接辞には、所属形相当の名詞的接頭辞、副詞的接頭辞、使役接尾辞（-yar）、複数接尾辞（-pa）がある。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-yar","-pa"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0134-04","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--the-causative-suffix-yar-ar-has-an-arity","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topics":["topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--causee"],"statement":{"en":"The causative suffix -yar / -ar has an arity of 0; the original subject is omitted and the causer becomes the new subject, forming a causative that does not express the causee.","ja":"使役接尾辞 -yar, -ar はアリティが 0 で、元の動詞の主語は消えて使役者が新たに主語となり、「〜に」を表示しない使役を作る。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-yar","-ar"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0198-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--in-causative-verbs-formed-with-yar-the-causee","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topics":["topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--causee"],"statement":{"en":"In causative verbs formed with -yar, the causee is non-specific ('anyone') and does not become a syntactic object.","ja":"-yar が付加された使役動詞では、行為を行わせる相手は特定されず（「誰にでも」）、目的語として文に現れない。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-yar"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0428-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--depending-on-the-verb-the-agent-causee-of","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topics":["topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--causee"],"statement":{"en":"Depending on the verb, the agent/causee of the base verb in a -yar/-ar causative can be specified using relational phrases such as or peka, or un, or eun.","ja":"動詞によっては、-yar/-ar による使役文でもとの動詞の動作主にあたるものを or peka、or un、eun などの形式を用いて指定することができる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"exists","modality":"possible","conditions":["特定の動詞において"]},"forms":["or peka","or un","eun","-ar","-yar"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0429-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--the-suffix-y-ar-is-a-suppletive-plural","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topics":["topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--causee"],"statement":{"en":"The suffix -(y)ar is a suppletive plural causative suffix that marks plurality of the causee.","ja":"接尾辞 -(y)ar は被使役者の複数を標示する補充的な複数使役接尾辞である。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-(y)ar"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0033-08","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--the-causee-deriving-from-an-intransitive-subject-does","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topics":["topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--causee"],"statement":{"en":"The causee deriving from an intransitive subject does not trigger the plural causee suffix -yar, being treated like the direct object of a transitive clause.","ja":"自動詞主語に由来する被使役者は複数被使役者接尾辞-yarを誘起せず、他動詞節の直接目的語と同様に扱われる。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":["intransitive clause base"]},"forms":["-yar"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0034-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--unlike-the-causative-suffix-re-the-causative-suffix","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topics":["topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--contrast"],"statement":{"en":"Unlike the causative suffix -re, the causative suffix -yar inherently includes the meaning of an unspecified causee and therefore cannot take a separate noun phrase indicating the causee as an object.","ja":"使役接尾辞 -yar は -re と違って不特定の被使役者の意味を同時に含んでいるため、被使役者を意味する名詞句を目的語として別に取ることはできない。"},"type":"distribution","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"none","modality":"necessary","conditions":["with causative suffix -yar"]},"forms":["-yar","-re"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0268-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--the-causative-suffix-yar-is-realized-as-yar","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topics":["topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--form"],"statement":{"en":"The causative suffix -yar is realized as -yar after stems ending in vowels and as -ar after stems ending in consonants.","ja":"使役接尾辞 -yar は、母音で終わる語幹の後では -yar、子音で終わる語幹の後では -ar として実現する。"},"type":"alternation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-yar","-ar"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaeva2022@handbook-epub/l0134-19","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--the-causative-suffix-allomorph-yar-occurs-after-sounds","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topics":["topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--form"],"statement":{"en":"The causative suffix allomorph -yar occurs after sounds other than r, while -ar occurs after r.","ja":"使役接尾辞 -yar, -ar は、r 以外の音の後では -yar、r の後では -ar となる。"},"type":"alternation","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"necessary","conditions":[]},"forms":["-yar","-ar"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0198-02","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--in-the-ishikari-dialect-the-suffix-yar-attaches","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topics":["topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--form"],"statement":{"en":"In the Ishikari dialect, the suffix -yar attaches to the causative form marked by -re/-te and functions as a double causative expressing that the causer makes someone cause the causee to do something.","ja":"石狩方言において接尾辞-yarは規則使役接尾辞-re/-teが付加された使役形に後続し、使役者が仲介者を使って被使役者に何かをさせる二重使役表現として用いられる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:hokkaido/central/ishikari"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-yar","-re","-te"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0034-04","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--the-indefinite-causative-suffix-yar-ar-encodes-only","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topics":["topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--semantics"],"statement":{"en":"The indefinite causative suffix -yar/-ar encodes only indirect causation.","ja":"不特定使役接尾辞-yar/-arは間接的使役のみを表す。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-yar","-ar"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:bugaevakobayashi2022@handbook-epub/l0100-31","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--the-indefinite-causative-suffix-yar-ar-adds-a","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topics":["topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--semantics"],"statement":{"en":"The indefinite causative suffix -yar ~ -ar adds a causer as the new subject but removes the original subject from the clause, leaving the verb's arity unchanged (+0).","ja":"不定使役接尾辞 -yar ~ -ar は使役者を新たな主語として加えるが、元の文の主語は文から除外されるため、動詞のアリティを変化させない（アリティ0）。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"all","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-yar","-ar"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:nakagawa2024@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0428-01","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--ainu-possesses-a-causative-suffix-yar-that-actively","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topics":["topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--semantics"],"statement":{"en":"Ainu possesses a causative suffix -yar that actively indicates that the direct agent/causee of the action is an unspecified person.","ja":"アイヌ語には行為の直接的な主体が不特定の人であることを積極的に示す使役の形式 (-yar) がある。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"unstated","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-yar"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:sato2008@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0267-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--the-plural-causative-suffix-y-ar-is-used","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topics":["topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--semantics"],"statement":{"en":"The plural causative suffix -(y)ar is used when the causee is indeterminate and not overtly expressed, without increasing the valency of the verb.","ja":"複数使役接尾辞-(y)arは被使役者が不特定で明示されない場合に用いられ、動詞の結合価を増加させない。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":["causee is indeterminate and not overtly expressed"]},"forms":["-(y)ar"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0034-02","stance":"reports"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
{"id":"claim:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--the-causative-suffix-y-ar-is-used-as","revision":1,"topic":"topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topics":["topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar","topic:valency/permissive-sociative-causative-yar--semantics"],"statement":{"en":"The causative suffix -(y)ar is used as an honorific causative expression directing respect toward the causee.","ja":"使役接尾辞-(y)arは被使役者に敬意を向ける敬語使役表現として用いられる。"},"type":"form-function","scope":{"doculects":["doculect:ainu"],"quantifier":"generic","modality":"actual","conditions":[]},"forms":["-(y)ar"],"statements":[{"id":"stmt:shibatani1990@gemini-3-flash-preview/l0034-03","stance":"asserts"}],"relations":[],"grouped_by":"act:group/2026-09-26T07-52-28-143Z","status":"grouped"}
